>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `REFUTE_TAC_WITH`

``` hol4
Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH : config_update list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample under per-call configuration updates.

`REFUTE_TAC_WITH updates` is `REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC cfg`, where `cfg` is
the stored configuration of the context the tactic is applied in, with
`updates` applied from left to right.  The stored configuration is
unchanged.

### Failure

Fails if an update fails or the resulting `expect` field is not met.

### Example

>>__ load "Refute";
>> g `!xs : num list. LENGTH xs < 3`;

>> e (Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH
        [Refute.upd_search (Refute.Only [Refute.Exhaustive]),
         Refute.upd_size 5]);
>>__ drop();

### See also

[`Refute.REFUTE_TAC`](#Refute.REFUTE_TAC),
[`Refute.REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC`](#Refute.REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC),
[`Refute.config`](#Refute.config).
